body:
Fixes #167077

## What Problem This Solves

Fixes Claude CLI conversations forking into stale branches when channel messages and `chat.send` alternate in the same session.

## User Impact

Every turn continues the latest native conversation, regardless of its inbound route. Account-private standing approvals remain isolated. No configuration, protocol, schema, or migration changes are required.

## Why This Change Was Made

The warm-process registry and queue included the inbound account and auth profile in their owner key, allowing one conversation to retain competing processes. Both now use conversation identity. Account changes participate in the existing process compatibility fingerprint, so the runtime retires and awaits the previous process before resuming. Approval grants are available only to the prepared turn that owns the activated process.

Thanks @cmatrx0 for the report. The separate manual-compaction retirement repair is tracked in #157766; session reset still creates a distinct conversation identity.

## Evidence

Fresh Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01m4dpr64s8mgtk0m5b3nnc741` ([workflow](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/37775020452)), Node 24.19.0 / pnpm 12.5.1, live-proof tree `9b5d1cd0a6f39935eab8f2a6a2d329d53cf82683`. Final tested/reviewed tree: `77cdeb388676205ba142c62ea20dc7aaafc2b602`; the only later changes removed four obsolete fields from two test expectations. Production bytes are identical:

| Real Gateway campaign | Successful turns | Maximum warm processes | Stale-parent forks |
| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
| Main `b925148b83b7ebddb32e1dd68769d6588d16f800` | 6 | 2 | 4 |
| Candidate | 6 | 1 | 0 |

All measured processes used `--resume` for the same seeded native session. Every owned process exited after each campaign. Main took 236.97s; candidate took 242.97s. The full remote proof command returned `LIVE_PROOF_PASS` and exit 0.

- Regression first: both new cases failed on unmodified main. Fresh-machine negative control restored only production files and again failed both cases at the missing-current-process assertion (33.92s); candidate tests pass.
- `pnpm test src/agents/cli-runner/cli-live-session-registry.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: 43 passed, 35.01s wall.
- `pnpm test src/agents/cli-runner/execute-plugin.test.ts --maxWorkers=1`: 38 passed, 27.36s wall. File wall times are mostly transform/import work; test bodies account for approximately 1% and 4% respectively.
- All 68 selected CLI-runner/command/runtime test files have passing results across the bounded runs, including `extensions/anthropic/cli-runtime.test.ts` (36 tests). The broad run caught two stale lookup expectations in `prepare.test.ts` and `attempt-execution.cli.test.ts`; their obsolete account/auth fields were removed, and both full files passed (115 and 77 tests). The last four-file run passed in 109.02s; updated `agents-other` and `commands` test-type graphs passed afterward.
- Remote `pnpm tsgo:core` and `pnpm tsgo:core:test --changed-paths-json '["src/agents/cli-runner/cli-live-session-registry.test.ts","src/agents/cli-runner/execute-plugin.test.ts","src/gateway/gateway-cli-backend.live.test.ts"]'` passed (`agents-other` and `gateway-root`). Local core and all 27 core test graphs also passed.
- Changed-file lint, formatting, diff checks, documentation sanity, ownership/ratchet guards, schema guard, import-cycle check, and the remaining changed gates passed.

`check:changed` remains red on two inherited unused exports: `SessionPendingInputState` in `src/config/sessions/session-accessor.sqlite-pending-inputs.ts`, and `discardStreamSegmentIndexes` in `ui/src/pages/chat/stream-segment-pruning.ts`. The same scan failed on the exact clean main tree in Testbox (103.97s), with the identical findings. Those files are untouched; no ignore or baseline exception was added.

ClawSweeper's issue findings are covered by the route/auth regression, cleanup settlement and cancellation cases, standing-approval isolation, and the real-Gateway parent-chain comparison. The fixture below records native resume parents independently of the registry.

The live fixture uses a real isolated Gateway, public WebSocket RPCs, the bundled Anthropic runtime, and a fake `claude` executable with process-local transcript state. It alternates an `agent` request with a synthetic Telegram account route and ordinary `chat.send`; it does not contact Telegram or Anthropic. A seed turn and Gateway restart ensure every measured child launches with `--resume` of the same native session.

Independent Codex autoreview: scoped-clean through P2. Production change: +4/-14 lines (net -10); tests +72/-20; docs +2/-0. The changelog is release-owned and untouched.

PR CI is pending at publication; CI durations are not yet available. The Testbox lease is stopped after successful command completion.

